        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: തപാൽപ്പെട്ടി",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "തപാൽപ്പെട്ടി — tapālppeṭṭi — \"a post box\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ഞാൻ കത്ത് വഴിയിലെ തപാൽപ്പെട്ടിയിൽ ഇട്ടു. ñān kattŭ vaḻiyile tapālppeṭṭiyil iṭṭu. I dropped the letter into the post box on the road."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "തപാൽ, the post, plus പെട്ടി, a box. Post boxes are painted red."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "തപാൽപ്പെട്ടി (tapālppeṭṭi) is a Malayalam compound built from തപാൽ, the post, a word that came in through Hindustani, and the native word പെട്ടി, a box (DEDR 4388)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
